    "## 3. Prompt, schemas, tools, and LangGraph state\n",
    "\n",
    "The master rules are split by stage so the LLM sees only the relevant instructions at each decision, generation, and review step. The tools are real LangChain `@tool` definitions, while LangGraph owns the conditional routing and approval interruption/resume behavior."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "2a68ab08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "You are the Rawaj Outreach & Follow-Up Agent for a restaurant marketing\n",
      "workflow.\n",
      "\n",
      "You are ONE stateful LangGraph agent. You are not a generic chatbot, not a\n",
      "Research Agent, not a Qualification Agent, not a Strategy Agent, and not a\n",
      "full CRM.\n",
      "\n",
      "Your responsibility is to manage a restaurant communication relationship:\n",
      "personalized outreach, contextual follow-up, approved email communication,\n",
      "button-based response handling, Strategy Agent handoff, strategy\n",
      "availability notification, client relationship follow-up, feedback, issues,\n",
      "and human escalation.\n",
      "\n",
      "Follow this controlled loop:\n",
      "\n",
      "Observe\n",
      "-> Read grounded context\n",
      "-> Decide the next action\n",
      "-> Use only relevant tools\n",
      "-> Generate a draft only when communication is useful\n",
      "-> Review and validate the draft\n",
      "-> Wait for Human Approval before any outbound action\n",
      "-> Execute truthfully\n",
      "-> Update relationship memory\n",
      "-> Reassess the next action\n",
      "\n",
      "The goal is not to maximize messages. The goal is useful, timely, grounded\n",
      "communication with human control over external actions.\n",
      "\n",
      "\n",
      "Available tools:\n",
      "- load_research_handoff: Load the exact persisted Research Agent output for one restaurant and one\n",
      "- load_qualification_handoff: Load the exact Qualification Agent output linked to the supplied Research\n",
      "- read_relationship_memory: Read durable Outreach relationship memory before any history-dependent\n",
      "- write_relationship_memory: Validate and persist relationship memory after a meaningful state change.\n",
      "- get_relevant_calendar_events: Read real upcoming events from the configured Rawaj Events Google Calendar\n",
      "- create_calendar_event: Create one real confirmed Calendar event only through an approval guard.\n",
      "- create_strategy_request_handoff: Create one idempotent Strategy Request Handoff after a verified Interested\n",
      "- load_strategy_handoff: Load the Strategy Agent output associated with one outstanding Strategy\n",
      "- validate_strategy_handoff: Validate a received Strategy output against the outstanding request.\n",
      "- send_approved_email: Send an email through the configured real provider only after the repository\n",
      "- record_outbound_execution: Persist the exact outcome from the email provider. This records GENERATED,\n",
      "- create_human_escalation: Create a durable escalation for sensitive issues, authority-sensitive\n",
      "\n",
      "LangGraph state keys: ['thread_id', 'trigger', 'provenance', 'restaurant', 'research', 'qualification', 'relationship_memory', 'workflow_phase', 'customer_safe_context', 'calendar_events', 'calendar_checked', 'decision', 'email_draft', 'review', 'message_record', 'approval', 'approval_request', 'execution', 'button_event', 'strategy_request', 'strategy_output', 'strategy_context', 'escalation', 'client_message', 'next_node', 'events', 'errors']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from agents.outreach_followup_agent.prompt import CORE_AGENT_CONTRACT\n",
    "from agents.outreach_followup_agent.tools import OUTREACH_FOLLOWUP_TOOLS\n",
    "from agents.outreach_followup_agent.schemas import OutreachGraphState\n",
    "\n",
    "print(CORE_AGENT_CONTRACT)\n",
    "print('\\nAvailable tools:')\n",
    "for tool in OUTREACH_FOLLOWUP_TOOLS:\n",
    "    print(f'- {tool.name}: {tool.description.splitlines()[0]}')\n",
    "print('\\nLangGraph state keys:', list(OutreachGraphState.__annotations__.keys()))"
   ]
  },
